WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.692
Did you find that AI ad of Chippy funny?
That was hilarious, though, wasn't it?

00:00:03.692 --> 00:00:04.720
Wasn't that brilliant?

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:12.226
I found it, yes, fascinating. And if people
looked at the ad at the start, they will

00:00:12.226 --> 00:00:14.900
have seen that it was an AI ad.

00:00:14.960 --> 00:00:19.987
It was fictional. That's what it said. It
was quite honest and upfront, but it was

00:00:19.987 --> 00:00:20.600
brilliant.

00:00:21.880 --> 00:00:26.520
And it cost, apparently, 200 bucks to make.

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:27.380
Amazing, eh?

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:32.561
You know, and they say that if you were
making it from scratch, it would cost well

00:00:32.561 --> 00:00:36.920
into six figures because you'd have to hire
actors and what have you.

00:00:37.300 --> 00:00:44.240
The really, I guess, determining feature of
whether it was [unclear] Chippy or not,

00:00:44.240 --> 00:00:51.097
was the rear vision mirror and the fact that
he climbed into the passenger door of

00:00:51.097 --> 00:00:54.860
the car and ended up driving away in the
car.

00:00:54.860 --> 00:00:58.380
Oh, yeah, there is no, I mean, there were AI
mistakes all over the show.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:01.609
When I watched it a second time, I realised
it, like, he's running in the day, then

00:01:01.609 --> 00:01:04.400
he bursts into the house and looks like
they're having dinner at night time.

00:01:05.060 --> 00:01:05.460
Yes, exactly.

00:01:05.460 --> 00:01:08.808
And then he's out again and it's daytime and
then he runs to the wrong side of the

00:01:08.808 --> 00:01:10.400
vehicle because it's an American video.

00:01:10.460 --> 00:01:11.820
And then drives off.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:12.760
Yeah, yeah, yeah.

00:01:13.220 --> 00:01:16.360
And it drives off on the right side of the
vehicle for us.

00:01:16.360 --> 00:01:18.300
But when he looks in the rear vision
mirror...

00:01:18.300 --> 00:01:19.380
Ethically, any problems?

00:01:19.500 --> 00:01:20.100
It's not him.

00:01:20.160 --> 00:01:22.240
It's a youthful Chippy.

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:25.220
No, I don't see any great problems.

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:27.080
You can't take something like that
seriously.

00:01:27.180 --> 00:01:27.400
Neither.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:27.860
We're going to...

